      "message": "I might be wrong but thought of checking: In debug mode base is actually an offset and not a VA right? I was reading the code in pkvm_init.c:pkvm_setup_percpu()\n```\n#ifndef CONFIG_PKVM_X86_DEBUG\n        nr_pages \u003d pkvm_sym(pkvm_per_cpu_nr_pages)();\n        if (!nr_pages)\n                return 0;\n\n        per_cpu_base \u003d pkvm_sym(pkvm_early_alloc_contig)(nr_pages);\n        if (!per_cpu_base || pkvm_sym(pkvm_setup_per_cpu)(cpu, __pa(per_cpu_base),\n                                      __pa(pcpu), __pa(vcpu))) {\n                pr_err(\"no percpu page for CPU%d\\n\", cpu);\n                return -ENOMEM;\n        }\n#else\n        /*\n         * Overwrite the pkvm\u0027s percpu setup symbols with the host percpu value\n         * as the same percpu base will be used by the pKVM and the host in the\n         * debug build.\n         */\n        if (pkvm_sym(pkvm_setup_per_cpu)(cpu, __per_cpu_offset[cpu],\n                                         __pa(pcpu), __pa(vcpu))) {\n                pr_err(\"no percpu page for CPU%d\\n\", cpu);\n                return -ENOMEM;\n        }\n#endif\n```\n\nIn debug mode, the second argument is `__per_cpu_offset[cpu]` which the offset in host I guess. That might be the reason we are assigning it directly to pkvm\u0027s `__per_cpu_offset[cpu]`. \n\nIf thats the case, a slight rewording of the comment would make it clea, probablys omething like:\n```\n  /*\n   * In debug mode, pKVM shares the host\u0027s per-CPU areas.\n   * Pass the host\u0027s per-CPU offset directly.\n   */\n``",
